The <ansi fg="command">server</ansi> command can be used in the following ways:

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">server stats</ansi> (or <ansi fg="command">server info</ansi>)
  Get stats on the server.

  <ansi fg="command">server set</ansi>
  Lists all server configuration settings.

  <ansi fg="command">server set [name] [value]</ansi>
  Sets a configuration setting (and saves it).

  <ansi fg="command">server set day</ansi> / <ansi fg="command">server set night</ansi>
  Force the game time to day or night.

  <ansi fg="command">server config</ansi>
  Initiates an interactive configuration editor.

  <ansi fg="command">server reload-ansi</ansi>
  Reloads aliases from the ansi alias file.

  <ansi fg="command">server ansi-strip</ansi> / <ansi fg="command">server ansi-mono</ansi> / <ansi fg="command">server ansi-normal</ansi>
  Debug toggles for ansi rendering: strip all color, monochrome,
  or restore normal output.
